d": 337114, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc784a.jpg"}, {"id": 1935389, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15hct.jpg"}, {"id": 1935390, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15hcu.jpg"}, {"id": 1935391, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15hcv.jpg"}, {"id": 1935392, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15hcw.jpg"}, {"id": 1935393, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15hcx.jpg"}, {"id": 1935394, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc15hcy.jpg"}], "slug": "bishoujo-janshi-suchie-pai", "storyline": "At the Game Center \"You&Me\", clerk Misaki Kyoko is a beginner of mahjong. However, with the Suchie pendant, developed by her father, she transforms into a \"Suchie-Pai\" a professional skilled mahjong fighter. Fight today for love, justice and peace!", "summary": "A Super Famicom mahjong game and the first title in the Idol Janshi Suchie-Pai mahjong series.\n\nBishoujo Janshi Suchie-Pai (\"Pretty Fighter Suchie-Pai\") is the first game in what would later be referred to as the Idol Janshi Suchie-Pai series. It's a mahjong game that uses comedy and attractive women to stand out among its more serious peers. The player, as the transforming warrior Suchie-Pai, can move around a world map to challenge various other female characters at mahjong in any order.\n\nThe characters were designed by Kenichi Sonoda, a famous animator and manga artist best known for the anime and manga Gunsmith Cats, who also worked on Bubblegum Crisis and Gall Force.", "themes": [{"id": 27, "name": "Comedy"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/bishoujo-janshi-suchie-pai", "videos": [{"id": 30732, "name": "Gameplay video", "video_id": "UvYXnIUxX_4", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UvYXnIUxX_4", "title": "Super Nintendo - Bishoujo Janshi Suchie-Pai (1993)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UvYXnIUxX_4/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 197976, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_